25
00:03:55,000 --> 00:04:02,000
The implants used for implant treatment are usually these three.

26
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:10,000
First, the external type implant austem has the brabd bane US for this type.

27
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:15,000
The connection between the fixture and the abutment is located outside.

28
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:19,000
This is the structure of the external implant.

29
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:24,000
The structure in the fixture is called the module.

30
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:33,000
If you look at the crystal module there is the hexagonal top on the platform. The hexagonal top will be connected to on abutment.

31
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:43,000
On top of it, the connection between the fixture and the abutment is located outside.

32
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:49,000
Such connection has some problems like this.

33
00:04:49,000 --> 00:05:02,000
The connection is outside that means microleakage can occur leading to the resorption of bone like this.

34
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:08,000
Another problem is the difficulty in doing the surgery.

35
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:16,000
When the bone height is not consistent in the surgical area and the height of consecutive fixtures is not appropriate.

36
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:21,000
The height of bone will converge to the low bone height.

37
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:27,000
The marginal bone of the implant placed in the higher bone is often resolved.

38
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:35,000
When the bone height is not consistent depending on the location of the fixture and how bone graft is done. 

39
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:42,000
The outcome may become fatal. Thus, the difficulty in surgery.

40
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:49,000
The biggest weakness of the external implants the marginal bond absorption is overcome. 

41
00:05:49,000 --> 00:06:02,000
With a tissue level implant, I don’t know if it was devised to address the problem. The cuff part of the abutment is included in the fixture body of tissue level implant.

42
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:07,000
This is the structure of the tissue level implant.

43
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:12,000
The crystal module looks different from the external type.

44
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:18,000
Then what has changed.

45
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:21,000
Broadly, four things can be discussed.

46
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:25,000
First, one piece implant.

47
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:31,000
Second, the implant is placed at the tissue level. The gingival level. 

48
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:38,000
Third, the connection between the fixture and the abutment is located inside the fixture.

49
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:50,000
Fourth, the connection between the fixture and the abutment is tapered.

50
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:57,000
The structure of the fixture does have changed. I've overcome the disadvantages of the external type.

51
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:05,000
In the one piece structure the prosthesis is connected at the gingival level.

52
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:09,000
So there is no microleakage.

53
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:23,000
And the appropriate soft tissue can be secured and abutment fixture connection part is inside the fixture so it leads to less micro movement and less screw loosening.

54
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:33,000
Therefore, marginal bone stability has been achieved evidence by many papers.

55
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:40,000
Actually, very good clinical outcome has been achieved.

56
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:46,000
So the tissue level implant has very good outcome.

57
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:52,000
So, one body incorporating the abutment in the fixture emerged.

58
00:07:52,000 --> 00:08:00,000
The screw connection between the fixture and the abutment has been completely eliminated.

59
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:08,000
There are advantages with that but if implant positioning is a little bit off, fabricating prosthesis is very difficult.

60
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:17,000
And when you need a bone grafting two-stage surgery is necessary but it is not possible with this implant.

61
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:30,000
Therefore, it is only used in a narrow region like a lower anterior or to fabricate a provisional tool or to maintain a denture.

62
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:40,000
So it is using a limited scope. The one body incorporating the abutment is not really used widely.

63
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:49,000
As implant transitioned from the external to tissue level implant there has been many advantages.

64
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:53,000
But, there are about three limitations. First,

65
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:58,000
The prostetic option limitation.

66
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:04,000
When the inner arch distance is short the implanted cuff is hard to adjust. 

67
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:13,000
Prosthetic shape is not very good they can fall off frequently.

68
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:19,000
Two, in the aesthetic area the abutment cannot be adjusted.

69
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:23,000
Therefore, aesthetically it is challenging.

70
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:33,000
Third, when the height of bone is not consistent. If the implant is placed based on the higher bone level like medial,

71
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:36,000
Threads of the implant are exposed at the distal side.

72
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:44,000
If you place an implant based on lower bone level at the distal side, it is placed too deep at the mesial side. 

73
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:50,000
So it is very challenging to determine the vertical positions of the fixture during surgery.

74
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:58,000
It feels uncomfortable to expose the threads. So mostly they are placed a  little deep like this.

75
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:09,000
If you place an implanted deep, that should not go deep like near the adjacent tooth you will not feel comfortable with it. 

76
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:23,000
In actual clinical setting the acutal tissue level implant is placed very deep which results in deep bone resorption. 

77
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:29,000
In another case, the tissue level implant is placed at the bone level.

78
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:41,000
Severe bone resorption occurred. So there are many advantages but surgical and prosthetic limitations exist. 

79
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:50,000
For the tissue level implant. The problem of the tissue level implant. The abutment cuff which is part of the fixture removed. 

80
00:10:50,000 --> 00:11:02,000
And the advantage of the implant which is the internal connection is adapted in the internal submerged implant.

81
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:07,000
It brings greater surgical convenience to dentists.

82
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:16,000
It has various prosthetic options, excelletn aesthetic solution and the breakthrough design.

83
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:21,000
The platform switching design and it is most widely used currently.

84
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:29,000
When there is inconsistent bone level, unlike the conventional implants like external or tissue level implants.

85
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:36,000
Stability in the marginal bone is achieved which was hard to get before. 

86
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:41,000
Internal submerged implant structure.

87
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:50,000
Internal structure and platform switching are the characteristics of the crystal module, looks like this.

88
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:57,000
Internal submerged type implant and the tissue level implant.

89
00:11:57,000 --> 00:12:02,000
Fixtures have the internal connection with the abutment that is the same but, 

90
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:15,000
The internal connection shape is different. The hex versus octa tissue level implant. The abutment connection. 

91
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:25,000
There is a stop at the fixture but in the internal submerged implant there is no such stuff due to the difference. 

92
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:30,000
The internal submerged implants have many problems.

93
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:40,000
There's a high risk of fracture due to thinner wall of the fixture.

94
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:46,000
Second, the abutment connection structure does not have a stop. 

95
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:49,000
Therefore, sink down can occur.

96
00:12:49,000 --> 00:13:02,000
Third, In thin biotype if the implant is placed shallow and fatal bone resorption can occur that is the disadvantage of the intra-submerged implant.

97
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:08,000
Let's look at how body types have change. 

98
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:15,000
At the beginning, the body of implant mostly were straight.

99
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:23,000
When bone quality is good that's not a problem but when the bone quality is weak initial stability is low and

100
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:34,000
and creates a problem for implant healing in order to address that implant has been made a tapered.

101
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:37,000
In order to increase the initial stability and the healing.

102
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:50,000
The straight fixture as you can see here. The first thread is passing and the other threads are following the thread.

103
00:13:50,000 --> 00:14:06,000
Therefore, the torque is maintained the consistent. The taper body type fixture when placing the implant high torque is achieved due to tapered shape and self-tapping capacity.

104
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:14,000
It is advantageous for early loading and immediate placement.

105
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:20,000
Taper body type fixture shows a higher contact with the bone.

106
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:35,000
Therefore, this fixture can create higher initial stability. Please keep that in mind and then you will be able to understand better the process of implanted healing in the next lecture.

107
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:48,000
Taper implant has another advantage, The implant apex passes through the entry point of the drilled hole reducing the installation time.

108
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:53,000
As you can see, the fixtures do not have interferance at the entrance.

109
00:14:53,000 --> 00:15:04,000
If it is a highly tapered double threaded implant it can be placed with just a three or four rotations.

110
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:10,000
 Another advantage of the taper type fixture is when bown becomes narrower.

111
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:24,000
The taper shape can prevent the damage to the roots of adjacent teeth as you can see in the picture.

112
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:32,000
Currently, there are various degree of taper but tapered body implants are mainly used.

113
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:44,000
next implant materials. 

114
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:50,000
The requirement for the implant materials most important one is the biocompatibility.

115
00:15:50,000 --> 00:16:01,000
Biocompatibilty means it should not cause inflamatory reaction in the body and it should not interfere with the cell growth. 

116
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:11,000
No matter how good the physical property may be. It should not generate any harmful effect in the body.

117
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:16,000
Professor Purunemak got the idea of using titanium while experimenting with rabbits.

118
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:22,000
Now, a lot of titanium implants are produced. 

119
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:33,000
In the past, people thought pure titanium should be used only but where high strength is required titanium alloy

120
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:38,000
Including aluminum or vanadium is used. 

121
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:50,000
Recently Zirconia including alloy is being developed I cannot cover all of them. Today I'm going to focus on the titanium which is most widely used material.

122
00:16:50,000 --> 00:17:00,000
Titanium is the most representative bioinert material when it goes into body there is no negative reaction to the tissue.

123
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:07,000
In the body, it forms highly stabilized oxide film and it is highly corrosion resistant.

124
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:16,000
It is classified in degrees 1 through 4 depending on the contents of oxygen and iron.

125
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:25,000
Titanium is a metal so ion can come out that can work very adversely in a living body.

126
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:36,000
But, titanium in body forms a stabilized oxide layer. It's thickness is about 200 nanometer.

127
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:47,000
The oxide layer enables the osseointegration so titanium it can be used as a safe materials for implants.

128
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:56,000
People used to think pure titanium can be used only but as a higher strength material is required for implants.

129
00:17:56,000 --> 00:18:01,000
Titainum alloy with aluminum and vanadium was developed. 

130
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:10,000
So grade 1 to 4 are pure titanium and grade 5 is alloy titanium.

131
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:21,000
From grade 1 to grade 5, In that direction the strength goes up but biocompatibility is decreased.

132
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:29,000
On the contrary , as you go toward the grade one strength would go down but biocompatibility will increase.

133
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:37,000
There used to be huge controversy over pure titanium vs alloy but it has subsided.

134
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:51,000
Right now, where high strength is required the small diameter implants or superstructure abutment or screws use grade 5 titanium.

135
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:56,000
And in other parts grade 4 titanium is used. 

